        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25009929?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is my best guess at what this book is, but I could be wrong, since this does not seem to be stated anywhere...</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3767",
            "title": "Book should say what it is about",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-06T22:38:05.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-01-31T13:23:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hkBst",
                "url": "https://github.com/hkBst"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14171107?u=ce02dd40378c3083f74de5ed504bb8a3161f8d90&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">RealtimeSanitizer is an approach to detecting real-time safety violations in timing critical code. It has been added to LLVM 20, adn this RFC aims to leverage that work and add it to Rust.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See the document for more.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for considering,<br>\nChris (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/cjappl/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/cjappl\">@cjappl</a>), David (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/davidtrevelyan/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/davidtrevelyan\">@davidtrevelyan</a>), and Stephen (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/steckes/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/steckes\">@steckes</a>)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/cjappl/rfcs/blob/rtsan_proposal/text/3766-rtsan-and-attributes.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3766",
            "title": "RFC: Implement RealtimeSanitizer (RTSan) support, add `#[realtime(nonblocking)]`, `#[realtime(blocking)]` attributes",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-23T09:43:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-01-30T23:34:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "cjappl",
                "url": "https://github.com/cjappl"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332036?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Please remember to create inline comments for discussions to keep this RFC manageable and discussion trees resolveable.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/oli-obk/rfcs/blob/const-trait-impl/text/0000-const-trait-impls.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tracking:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"544416304\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/67792\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/67792/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/67792\">rust-lang/rust#67792</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3762",
            "title": "Make trait methods callable in const contexts",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-21T10:11:43.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-01-13T16:44:06.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "oli-obk",
                "url": "https://github.com/oli-obk"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76854355?u=c8a002ee3c70f41a556c7dff250e0abf1244ec76&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h1 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The addition of <code class=\"notranslate\">supported-targets</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">Cargo.toml</code>. This field is an array of <code class=\"notranslate\">target-triple</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">cfg</code> specifications that restricts the set of targets which a package supports. Packages must meet the <code class=\"notranslate\">supported-targets</code> of their dependencies, and they can only be built for targets that satisfy their <code class=\"notranslate\">supported-targets</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/carloskiki/rfcs/blob/master/text/3759-cargo-supported-targets.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3759",
            "title": "RFC: Allow packages to specify a set of supported targets",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-28T08:39:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-01-08T19:43:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "carloskiki",
                "url": "https://github.com/carloskiki"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6120103?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Special case struct patterns containing only a rest pattern (e.g., <code class=\"notranslate\">Foo { .. }</code>) so that they can match values of any type with the appropriate name, not just structs (e.g., it could match an <code class=\"notranslate\">enum Foo</code> value). This is done so that structs containing only private fields can be changed to other types without breaking backwards compatibility.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/rest-patterns-foo-should-match-non-struct-types/21607\" rel=\"nofollow\">Prior discussion on IRLO</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/theemathas/rfcs/blob/rest_pattern_matches_non_struct/text/3753-rest-pattern-matches-non-struct.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3753",
            "title": "RFC: `Foo { .. }` pattern matches non-struct types",
            "date_modified": "2025-01-10T15:09:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-31T10:47:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "theemathas",
                "url": "https://github.com/theemathas"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4459874?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC is largely the work of <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/rylev/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/rylev\">@rylev</a> and <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/chriswailes/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/chriswailes\">@chriswailes</a>. As <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3379#issuecomment-1876158423\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3379/hovercard\">suggested by @tmandry</a> I have stripped it down to an MVP that just adds <code class=\"notranslate\">os_version_min</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisDenton/rfcs/blob/os-min-version/text/3750-cfg-os-version-min.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3750",
            "title": "RFC: cfg_os_version_min",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-11T13:59:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-27T11:09:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ChrisDenton",
                "url": "https://github.com/ChrisDenton"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/653604?u=bcaaafaa0439ac0006d5e4aff450ab0b826bc5ec&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Add a new environment variable <code class=\"notranslate\">CARGO_CHECK</code> that is set to <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> when running <code class=\"notranslate\">cargo check</code> so build scripts can skip expensive compilation steps that are unnecessary for Rust type checking, such as compiling external C++ code in cxx based projects.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/akiselev/rfcs/blob/cargo-check-env/text/3748-cargo_check_environment_variable.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3748",
            "title": "RFC: Set CARGO_CHECK environment variable when type checking",
            "date_modified": "2025-01-04T11:41:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-21T04:51:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "akiselev",
                "url": "https://github.com/akiselev"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185516564?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">issue for this RFC <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/134475\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/134475/hovercard\">rust-lang/rust#134475</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes checking for <code class=\"notranslate\">T: Sized</code> in required trait methods (which do not check for some reason) which will be a future compatibility lint</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/ionicmc-rs/rfcs/blob/master/text/3696-unsized-params-in-traits.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3745",
            "title": "unsized params in traits",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-25T19:59:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-18T21:11:39.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ionicmc-rs",
                "url": "https://github.com/ionicmc-rs"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128307220?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">As discussed previously:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://smallcultfollowing.com/babysteps/blog/2014/05/13/focusing-on-ownership/\" rel=\"nofollow\">2014 Blog post</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/lack-of-mut-in-bindings-as-a-deny-by-default-lint/15818\" rel=\"nofollow\">2021 IRLO thread</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/213817-t-lang/topic/Idea.3A.20Downgrade.20.22immutable.20variable.E2.80.9C.20errors.20to.20lints\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zulip thread</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mutation of non-mutable locals arguably resembles a lint more than a hard error.  Converting it to a configurable lint has the potential to reduce friction and more clearly distinguish it from Rust's more fundamental type system restrictions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Implementing this is less effort than you might expect: the borrow checker already has separate code paths for handling local variables.  I've written a proof-of-concept for the change as part of <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/134233\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/pull/134233/hovercard\">this pull request</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/em-tg/rfcs/blob/emy/text/3742-mutate-non-mutable-locals.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3742",
            "title": "Convert \"reassignment of immutable local\" and \"mutable borrow of immutable local\" from a hard error to a deny-by-default lint",
            "date_modified": "2024-12-20T15:36:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-15T19:26:35.000Z",
